items.stem:
What is printed as a result of executing the following code segment?
```java
Playlist p = new Playlist();
p.add("Ada");
p.add("Bo");
p.add("Cy");
p.play();
p.play();
System.out.println(p.size() + " " + p.getPlays());
```

options.text:
```
public int averagePlays() {
        return plays / size();
    }
```

```
public int averagePlays() {
        return size() == 0 ? 0 : plays / size();
    }
```

```
public int averagePlays() {
        return size() / plays;
    }
```

```
public int averagePlays() {
        return plays * size();
    }
```

items.explanation_en:
The correct answer is:
```
public int averagePlays() {
        return size() == 0 ? 0 : plays / size();
    }
```
The conditional avoids dividing by zero for an empty playlist and otherwise uses integer division of plays by the number of songs.
An incorrect option:
```
public int averagePlays() {
        return plays / size();
    }
```
Divides without checking for an empty playlist, which throws an ArithmeticException.
An incorrect option:
```
public int averagePlays() {
        return size() / plays;
    }
```
Divides the number of songs by the number of plays, in the wrong order.
An incorrect option:
```
public int averagePlays() {
        return plays * size();
    }
```
Multiplies instead of dividing.

